Fig. 13. Calculating the number of intersections of the profile at mean line.

3.6. Number of peaks in the profile (m)
This parameter calculates the number of peaks of the profile per unit length (centimetre or inch). Peaks are counted only when the distance between the current peak and the preceding one is greater that 10% of the maximum height of the profile (Rt). In Fig. 14 the three little peaks, which follow the peaks m2, m3 and m4 are neglected because the distance between each peak and the preceding one in too small.
Download: Download full-size image

Fig. 14. Calculating the number of peaks along the profile.

The number of peaks can be calculated from the following equation:
m=1L∑i=1nmi
where L is the profile length (in cm).
3.7. Number of inflection points (g)
This parameter calculates the number of inflection points of the profile per unit length (centimetre or inch). An inflection point occurs when the profile changes its direction at any point as shown in Fig. 15. This parameter can be calculated from the following equation:
g=1L∑i=1ngi
where L is the profile length (in cm).
